.TH CLOG10 3 "June 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
clog10, clog10f, clog10l \- complex base-10 logarithm
.SH LIBRARY
Math library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <complex.h>
.PP
.BI "double complex clog10(double complex " z );
.br
.BI "float complex clog10f(float complex " z );
.br
.BI "long double complex clog10l(long double complex " z );
.PP
Feature-test macro requirements (see
.BR feature_test_macros (7)):
.PP
.RS 4
.BR clog10 (),
.BR clog10f (),
.BR clog10l ():
.RS 4
_GNU_SOURCE
.RE
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR clog10 ()
function computes the base-10 logarithm of the complex number
.IR z .
It is defined as the natural complex logarithm scaled by the natural
logarithm of 10:
.PP
.RS 4
.BI "clog10(" z ") = clog(" z ") / ln(10)" .
.RE
.PP
Equivalently, writing
.I z
in the form
.IR "x + iy" ,
.PP
.RS 4
.BI "clog10(" z ") = (log10|" z "|) + i*(atan2(" y ", " x ") / ln(10))" ,
.RE
.PP
so the real part is the base-10 logarithm of the magnitude of
.I z
and the imaginary part is the argument (phase angle) of
.I z
expressed in units scaled by
.IR "1/ln(10)" .
.PP
There is a branch cut along the negative real axis, matching
.BR clog (3):
the imaginary part of the result lies in the interval
.RB [ \-pi/ln(10) ,\  +pi/ln(10) ].
.PP
The
.B f
and
.B l
suffixed variants
.RB ( clog10f (),
.BR clog10l ())
take and return
.B "float complex"
and
.B "long double complex"
values respectively.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR clog10 ()
returns the complex base-10 logarithm of
.IR z .
The special-value behaviour is inherited from
.BR clog (3)
(scaled by the real constant
.IR "1/ln(10)" ).
.SH ERRORS
No errors are reported through
.IR errno .
Exceptional conditions (for example a zero argument, which yields a
real part of
.B \-infinity
and raises a divide-by-zero condition in the underlying real
logarithm) are reported only through the floating-point environment by
the constituent
.BR clog (3)
computation.  See
.BR math_error (7)
and
.BR fetestexcept (3).
.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
.TS
allbox;
lb lb lb
l l l.
Interface	Attribute	Value
T{
.BR clog10 (),
.BR clog10f (),
.BR clog10l ()
T}	Thread safety	MT-Safe
.TE
.SH STANDARDS
None.  This is a GNU C library extension.
.SH HISTORY
A glibc extension; it complements the C99
.BR clog (3)
in the same way that
.BR log10 (3)
complements
.BR log (3)
for real arguments.
